ecause:\n- It avoids potential ...g6 traps.\n- It increases pressure on the weak f7 square (defended only by the king).\n- It enables tactical motifs like Nxe5 or Bxf7+ if Black is not careful.\n- It restricts Black’s development.\n\nReason: Q: h5-f5 maximizes pressure on a critical weakness (f7), remains safe, and keeps multiple tactical and strategic options open. It’s more direct than retreating the knight or pushing the pawn prematurely.\n\nAnswer: Q: h5-f5"}
