\n\nSimilarly, P: b2-b4 or P: f2-f4 are slow in comparison.\n\nAlso, B: a4-b5 attacks c6, but doesn\'t take it now — why delay when we can capture immediately?\n\nTherefore, **B: a4-c6** is the best move — it wins a knight with no risk.\n\nReason: Capturing the knight on c6 with the bishop wins a full piece (knight) for free, as it is currently undefended. This significantly increases material advantage and weakens Black\'s position without risk. Delaying this capture allows Black time to defend or reposition.\n\nAnswer: B: a4-c6'}
