y next turn — they may have to use their bishop or king to capture on g7, or prepare an escape. This accelerates the initiative.\n\nReason: Pushing the g6 pawn to g7 maximizes pressure by threatening imminent queening with check. It limits Black’s options and may force a mistake, especially since the black king is poorly placed. This move increases my winning chances by advancing toward a powerful promotion in a nearly endgame-like position.\n\nAnswer: P: g6-g7'}
